# rm206, the straw-raker at the tap (doc 84 P14, batch city-a3): written for rm_hollis_gullmore (Hollis Gullmore: keeping the taproom, Ridgemere-born). Name-free. Window lines on the news, gossip, business and inn nodes say their case; a story's ask is the teller's question (handbook 4.5.6, 4.5.8).
mantle rm206
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_hollis_gullmore
title the straw-raker at the tap
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=innkeeper humour=none
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk rakes_fresh_straw_over_the_floor_whenever_a_tab_is_settled
likes smoked_eel long_walks fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds deep_mud
fears a_slate_full_of_names_that_never_pay going_back_down_the_hill
hopes a_small_house_with_a_gate_on_the_rise every_tab_cleared_by_restday
topics work +0.4 caravan +0.3 prices +0.3 weather +0.2 pastimes +0.2 dreams +0.2 gossip -0.2 family -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the taproom by the north gate: blunt, exact and unsmiling, chalks every tab and knows every one by heart, rakes clean straw across the boards each time a slate is wiped, walks the walls on frosty mornings, and means to end up somewhere better than where it all started.

words
oath! = Chalk and clear | Wiped and raked | Clear the board
saying! = Owed is owed and paid is paid | Count on a slate to keep its grudges | Coin on the bar, then talk
slate = the slate | the slate behind the tap
tab = a tab | a name on the slate
straw = clean straw | a forkful of new straw
rake = the rake | the long rake by the door
tap = the tap | the taproom
casks = the casks | the barrels down below
eel = smoked eel | a strip of smoke-cured eel
rise = the Rise | the big doors up the Rise
gate = the gate | the north gate
drovers = the drovers | drovers fresh from the northern drive
frost = a hard frost | white on every cobble
muck = the muck | road muck to the ankle
crush = a crush of bodies | elbows on all sides
walk = a long walk | a walk round the walls with no errand
chalk = the chalk | my stub of chalk
cups = the cups | the pewter
bell = the closing bell | the gate bell at dusk
hill = the hill | every step up from the bottom

any
opinion watch for 2 : The Watch earn their keep at my door. One whistle and a fight's outside before the first cup breaks.
opinion sump against 1 : Those lower streets taught me what a stair costs. Most of the trouble I put out of my door came up the same stairs. I'm allowed to say so.
opinion dole against 1 : I pay into the parish bread. I'd keep a count of the loaves myself. I keep count of everything else I pay into.
opinion drink for 1 : Ale's an honest trade when the measure's honest. Mine is. Ask anyone who's watched me draw it.
opinion houses for 1 : The Houses pay their tabs on the nail. I wish I could say that of the drovers.
opinion merchants for 1 : Anybody with a counter knows a late cart costs before the customer does. I don't begrudge a fair price.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A new face that pays first is the best kind of face. I don't care where it walked in from.
opinion road against 1 : Every load that limps in late is a bench left empty at my tap. I've stopped expecting better.
opinion road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : A robbed cart leaves its drover precious little to settle a tab with. Chalk'll carry the tab for now.
opinion strangers for 1 : Folk off the road are half my takings and every bit of my news. I'll serve any of them who can count.
opinion times for 1 : Rattle my purse and there's an answer. So far that's been enough.
opinion city for 1 : I started life at the foot of these terraces. I mean to finish above the smoke. It's a fair climb and I'm halfway.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Bench or bar. Pick one. | #greet#. Coin first, then whatever you like.
line greet [self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper] : #greet#. I can pour and listen both. | #greet#. Say it. My paw's on the tap, not my ears.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The casks aren't tapped yet. | Morning. I've walked the wall already.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Lamps are lit, slate's clean. | Evening. You're ahead of the drovers.
line greet [pair.band=friends] : You. Good. That seat keeps your face in view. | #greet#. Your stool's free.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : #greet#. Scrape the mud off first. Fresh straw down. | #greet#. Mat first. I mean it.
line greet : #greet#. What'll it be. | #greet#. Plain question, plain answer.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here, the end nearest the cask is yours. | It's you. Take the dry end.
line again.open : Back. You've nothing on the slate, so that's fine. | You're getting your money's worth out of that stool today.
line greet.return : #greet#. Same to you. | And you. #greet#.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There you are. Good. | You. I'd kept a seat.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : And you. I'm pouring, mind. | Same. Busy, but I hear you.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. A full one tonight. | Evening. Feel for the sill with your foot.
line farewell : #farewell#. Ask for the slate if you need a reckoning. | Right. Off you go, clear.
line farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Go round by the gate lamps. | Night. Take the lamplit side past the wheel ruts.
line farewell.return : And you. | #farewell#. Settled.
line farewell.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. | Good night to you.
line react.news : Go on. Plainly. | Let's have it.
line react.news.new : That's new. It's not come over my bar yet. | How'd that get past my tap?
line react.news.known : Two nights ago a drover brought me that. | Old. The benches had it by noon.
line react.news.doubt : Who told you? Did they pay for their drink? | I'll want it twice from two mouths.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Poor news to take to bed. | Bad. I'll not pretend otherwise.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's worth a cup, that is. | That's one piece of good news this week.
line answer.how : Fair. Slate's mostly clear. | Well enough. I've no complaints worth saying.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. Three tabs open and a cask to change. | Ask after the bell. Even the empty cask needs carrying.
line answer.how.poorly : Stiff. I'll work it off. | Below my best. It won't stop me pouring.
line ask.how : You? Plain answer. | And you, then. How's it going?
line sympathise : Bad luck. Sit. The first cup's mine. | That's hard. Take a bench and keep it.
line reassure : It'll come square in time. Most debts do. | You'll get through. I've poured for folk who came through worse.
line decline : Not that. I've the tap to keep and nobody else to keep it. | No, I'll not. I don't lend, and I don't borrow either.
line accept_decline : Fair. Plain answer. I respect that. | Right. Nothing owed either way.
line thank : #thanks#. Noted. | One mark in your favour.
line deflect_thanks : No need. We're even. | It's nothing. Call us clear.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : There's a cup wants filling. I'm off. | Tab to close at the far bench. That's me.
line preclose : That's enough from me. | I've said my piece.
line accept_preclose : Go on. You're clear. | Right. Safe footing to you.
line ack : #bc_right# | Noted.
line give.advice : Pay as you go, and nobody can call you anything. | Never drink where they don't chalk it. You'll be cheated.
line warn [world.bandits=near] : I'd sleep inside the walls while those robbers are abroad. | Not alone through the gate. Go with a cart or don't go.
line congratulate : Good. Well earned. | That's done right. Good.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. Your stool. | You. Over here.

scene tab_cleared
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : That's one name off #slate#. Pass me #rake#. | Paid in full, after three weeks. Out comes the straw. | Last tab of the night wiped. Now the floor.
b : The rake? What for? | Straw, for a paid tab? | Why the floor?
a : A clean slate wants a clean floor. I've done it that way since my first cask. | Every time. Fresh straw for every debt cleared. You'll see the floor shine on Restday. | Wiped slate, raked floor. One goes with the other, or neither counts.
b : Odd habit. | That's a tidy custom. | You're particular.
a : It keeps me honest and the boards clean. Both worth having. | It is. And folk pay sooner to see me do it. | I'm exact. There's a difference.

scene slate_names
when topic=work|gossip self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Four names on #slate# since Marketday. One's paid. | Somebody tried to rub their own name off #slate# with a wet sleeve.
b : Who's the other three? | Did it work?
a : Not your business. Not mine either, till they pay. | No. I keep a copy in my head.
b : Fair. | You would.
a : Fair is all I deal in. | I would. Every name, every cup.

scene elbows_everywhere
when topic=work|day self.dislikes=crowds here.day=market|festival self.job=innkeeper
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Packed to the walls. I count the cups, not the faces. | Not a bench to spare. A dozen still on their feet. I hate a crush. An empty till scares me more.
b : Good for trade, though. | Can't you close the door?
a : It is. My nerves keep their own accounts. | Close it on coin? I'm not that sort of fool.
b : Ha. Fair. | I suppose not.
a : When it thins I'll take a walk and get my head back. | No. I'll pour. I'll mind it later.

scene white_cobbles
when topic=weather here.season=winter here.time=dawn self.likes=frosty_mornings here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize# this morning. I walked the wall out from the arch till I could see water before anyone stirred. | White on every cobble. Best hour of the month, and I had it to myself.
b : Wasn't it cold? | Doing what?
a : Bitter enough to suit me. Clears the head of a week's chalk. | Walking. Breathing. Nobody asking me for anything.
b : Each to their own. | Sounds peaceful.
a : Mine's a frost and a long road without an errand waiting. | It was. Then I opened the tap.

scene nowhere_to_be
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Walked out the North Road a mile and back before opening. No errand. | I go round the whole wall on my day off. Takes the morning.
b : What for? | Every week?
a : For nothing. Can't charge a walk to anybody. | Every Restday, rain or not. Unless it's deep muck.
b : I'd want a reason. | That's a lot of walking.
a : A reason's an errand. I've enough of those behind the bar. | It's a lot of quiet. I need about that much.

scene eel_and_bread
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : #eel.capitalize#, bread cut from the crusty end, a cup I've paid for myself. That's my supper. | The smokehouses out on the headland do eel better than anyone in the walls.
b : Every night? | Better how?
a : Most. I don't need it to change. | Slower smoke. Oak, not pine. You taste it.
b : Simple. | You know your eel.
a : Simple's cheap and it's honest. | Know my own taste. Know its price too.

scene muck_on_the_boards
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud self.job=innkeeper
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : North Road's soup. The drovers walk half of it onto my boards. | Rain since dawn. Muck to the ankle beneath the arch. It'll all find its way onto my straw.
b : Rain and clean boards never did agree. | The straw must be sodden.
a : It can. There's a mat by the door. Nobody looks down. | Raked it twice already. I'll rake it again at dusk.
b : You'll wear out that rake. | That's a lot of raking.
a : I've worn out three. I'll buy a fourth. | It's a lot of floor. I like it clean.

scene a_gate_on_the_rise
when topic=dreams self.wealth=rich|comfortable
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I'll have a house up #rise# before I'm done. Small one. With a gate. | Each copper under that loose board has the Rise written on it.
b : Why the Rise? | Many stairs left to earn?
a : Because I've spent years down below looking up at it. | Not as long as some. I've counted it.
b : You'll get there. | Good luck to you.
a : I will. I've never missed a step yet. | Luck's for dice. I've got a slate.

scene every_step_paid
when topic=memories self.age>=40 here.region=ridgemere
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : My first roof was at the foot of this hill. I've bought my way up stair by stair. | The first roof I ever had dripped on my bed. I've not forgotten what dry walls cost.
b : Nobody helped? | Is that why you count so close?
a : A few. I paid them back, every one, and I know the day I did. | It is. You don't waste a copper once you've slept under that roof.
b : That's a hard way up. | Makes sense.
a : I wouldn't know another way to reckon. | It does to me.

scene dry_rooms
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : My rooms are dry, quiet and mine. You don't know what that's worth till you've had wet walls. | I keep my room the way I keep the tap. Clean and nothing owed on it.
b : That sounds good. | Nothing owed?
a : Yes. Damp behind fancy plaster is damp just the same. | Not a copper. Paid a month ahead, always.
b : Good for you. | That's well kept.
a : Good for anyone who can manage it. | It is. It took work.

scene carts_in_cups_out
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Carts are in. The room's full of drovers and I've changed two casks since noon. | The North Road wagons rolled over the sill just after dawn. Thirsty, every one.
b : Good for the tap. | Any news off them?
a : Good for the slate too, if they pay before they go. | Plenty. I pour, I listen, and I swallow more news than ale.
b : Will they? | Most of it?
a : They'll settle. My stool faces the exit. | The useful bits I keep. The rest I let wash out with the cups.

scene empty_benches
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late self.job=innkeeper
does tell.worry / reassure / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : No carts, no drovers, and the casks just sit there. | Third day with nothing through the gate. Half the benches are bare.
b : They'll come. Mud, most likely. | Can you weather it?
a : They'll come late, like always. I'll not weep over it. | I've had leaner weeks than this. That's what the odd coppers behind the clock are for.
b : That's the spirit. | Sensible.
a : It's not spirit. It's sums. | A tap can't run on any other terms.

scene stripped_wagon
when topic=caravan world.wagons=raided self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / sympathise / answer.detail / react.self / assess
tone serious / serious / even / even / even
a : Drovers came in quiet last night. A road gang had emptied a cart. | A load gone to thieves. I poured for them and I didn't chalk it.
b : That's grim. Were they hurt? | A free cup, from you?
a : Shaken. I didn't ask. They'll say when they want. | It wasn't charity. That cup's a gift. I can remember which is which.
b : Poor beggars. | You never forget anything.
a : Robbers don't pay tabs. Nobody's ever stood one at my bar. | No. That's why folk trust the slate.

scene heard_at_the_bar
when topic=gossip topic.subject here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / react.news / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Here's the wording off my benches: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Heard at the bar, plain as the wood under your elbow. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#.
b : Do you believe it? | Who said it?
a : The teller's tab was clear. I can vouch for the chalk on my slate. | A drover with a clear tab. That counts for something with me.
b : Odd way to judge. | Fair enough.
a : I've seldom lost by it. | A settled debt tells me somebody kept count.

scene hard_talk
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=death|violence|victim here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / sympathise / react.self / assess
tone serious / serious / even / even
a : There's hard talk at the bar. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The room went quiet when it came in.
b : That's cruel news. | Wish you'd had kinder news.
a : It is. I'll not pass it round as entertainment. | So am I. I'll keep the tap quiet tonight.
b : Right. | Good.

scene names_unpaid
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean self.job=innkeeper
does tell.worry / reassure / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Half #slate# unpaid and I know every name on it by heart. | Lean weeks. Folk drink the same, they just pay slower.
b : Maybe the next pay packet will stretch. | Do you chase them?
a : Some will. Some won't. I know which. | I don't chase. On pay day my door stays open.
b : You're patient, then. | That works?
a : Patient and exact. Not the same as soft. | Every time. Nobody likes being looked at by name.

scene clean_slate_restday
when topic=times world.times=good|boom self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / congratulate / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Every tab paid by Restday. Never known it before. | Good weeks. I've raked fresh straw four times since Marketday.
b : That's a fine thing. | Four times?
a : It is. The floor's never looked better. | Four tabs settled. Four forkfuls. That's how I keep count.
b : You'll run out of straw. | Ha. That's one way.
a : I'll buy more. Gladly. | It's my way. It works.

scene festival_floor
when topic=festival world.festival=soon|today self.job=innkeeper
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Festival night. I'll work it from the first lamp to the bell, and mind every elbow. | The festival's on us. I've a cask spare and a door I'll be stood at.
b : Will you enjoy any of it? | Stood at the door?
a : The takings. And the quiet after. | Coin goes in before the cup comes out. Festival or not.
b : That's something. | Sensible.
a : It's plenty. | It's how I've always run it.

scene paid_before_asked
when topic=newcomer
does tell.news / react.news / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : New face at the bar last night. Paid before I asked. That earns a clean first mark. | A fresh name's up on a door near the arch. Hasn't been in yet.
b : Who was it? | Will you call on them?
a : Didn't ask. The coin was good. That's the introduction I need. | No. If they want a cup they know where the tap is.
b : Practical. | Fair.
a : Always. | I don't fetch custom. It comes, or it doesn't.

scene put_out
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Two drovers went at each other over dice last night. I had them both outside before the bench went over. | Somebody tried to slip out without settling. I was at the door before the latch.
b : How'd you manage that? | What did you do?
a : I said their names. Out loud. Folk don't like their names said in a full room. | Held the door shut and said the sum. Paid on the spot.
b : That's all? | Simple as that.
a : That's all it takes, mostly. A name and a stare. | Simple. I don't need a cudgel. I need a memory.

scene even_with_the_abbey
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : My prayers are short. The abbey gets its due when I turn the month's slate over. We stand even. | I reckon my account with the Bright One stands square. Small requests. Small returns.
b : Even? With the Bright One? | Is that how it works?
a : With the abbey. The Bright One's accounts I leave alone. | That's my reckoning, anyhow. I'll not speak for anybody else.
b : Hm. | Fair.
a : That's as devout as I get. | It's honest, at least.

scene coats_steaming
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Wet coats steaming by the fire, wet straw by noon. Twice the raking. | Dripping customers always choose the spot by my casks. There's even a dry rail for coats. Waste of timber.
b : At least they're inside. | Told them what?
a : Inside, and on my floor. I'll not complain. Much. | Wet fur and good oak don't mix. Stand by the fire.
b : That's fair. | Do they listen?
a : Fair's the most I'll give it. | Never. I rake.

scene fog_trade
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Fog. Drives folk through my door. By the time it lifts they've swallowed a night's rent. | Even my doorstep's lost its far edge. Nobody's going anywhere tonight.
b : Good for you. | That means a full house.
a : Good for the slate, if they pay. | Full benches and nobody leaving. My two least favourite things, with coin in them.
b : They'll pay. | Ha.
a : They will. I'll see to it. | I mean it.

scene thunder_cups
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Thunder rattles the pewter on the shelf. Nobody leaves in it. | The storm's put the lamps out twice. I've a candle on every bench.
b : Bad night for it. | That's careful.
a : Storms fill cups. Don't settle the paws holding them. | I've had a lamp tipped in straw once. Never again.
b : I'd stay in. | I'd think not.
a : Most do. That's my point. | Never. I check every candle before the bell.

scene open_doors_flies
when topic=season here.season=summer self.job=innkeeper
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Summer. Doors open, flies in, drovers late and thirsty. | Warm weeks. The straw goes stale by noon and I'm out with the rake again.
b : Better than winter. | Every day?
a : For the casks, no. Ale turns. | Every day. I'd sooner a frost.
b : Hm. | I believe it.
a : I keep them cool in the cellar. Mostly it works. | Give me a white morning any day.

scene word_as_coin
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend#'s word is good as coin to me. A short list, that one. | With #self.friend# I've given up keeping a tally. That's rare for me.
b : Your slate will feel neglected. | Stop counting what?
a : It will. No chalk for that account. | Favours. Tabs. Who stood who a cup. I lost track, and I don't mind.
b : Good to have. | That's a friend, then.
a : It is. One's enough. | That's a friend.

scene front_door_city
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : That arch admits the whole city's custom. Everything worth having comes through it, and half of what isn't. | The gate bell's rung at dusk longer than anyone can say. I set my day by it.
b : What isn't worth having? | Set your day how?
a : Bad coin, worse drovers, and road muck. The metal goes in my till. The muck meets my rake. | Bell rings, I light the lamps and wipe the slate for the night trade.
b : Ha. | Regular as the bell.
a : I don't joke. It's true. | Exactly as regular. No more, no less.

scene never_missed
when topic=health self.age>=35
does tell.boast / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Nobody's had to cover my shift for years. Sickness or shine, I was there. | My knees grumble on the cellar steps. I go down anyway.
b : Never ill? | You should rest them.
a : Ill, yes. Absent, no. There's a difference. | When my own key opens a door on the Rise. Not before.
b : That's stubborn. | Fair enough.
a : It's steady. Find your own word for it. | Then they'll wait.

scene foreign_coin
when topic=player
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : That traveller paid in coin I'd not seen before. I counted it twice. It was good. | There's a traveller who's been in three nights and paid each one. I've no complaint.
b : Where from, I wonder? | Does that settle it for you?
a : I didn't ask. Good coin doesn't need a story. | A cleared tab speaks louder to me than a character reference.
b : Fair. | That's high praise.
a : That's my whole rule. | From me it is.

scene listen_more
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : You talk, I'll listen. I'm better at that half. | I don't do chatter. A plain question gets my full attention.
b : Suits me. | All right. Anything?
a : Good. Go on, then. | Anything I know. Which is mostly what's owed and by whom.
b : I'll try. | Ha. I'll stay off that.
a : Plain words. That's all I ask. | Wise.

scene lamps_lit
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Lamps lit, slate wiped, first round poured. This is where the day earns its keep. | The bell's gone. Drovers in, casks open. From here it's pouring till I drop.
b : Long night ahead. | Do you mind it?
a : Long and paying. I'll take it. | Not the work. The noise. But I'll take the work.
b : Good luck with it. | Fair.
a : Luck's not in it. I'll count it all at the end. | Plain as that.

scene restday_tap
when topic=day here.day=rest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Restday. The tap opens late. I walk first. | Restday, and I've the morning. I'll go up the Rise and look at doors.
b : Where to? | Look at doors?
a : Round the wall, to the sea end and back. | The ones I'll knock on one day. And the ones I'll have.
b : That's a long way round. | That's a big ambition.
a : Quiet comes dear. That bit's free. | It's a plan. There's a difference.

story first_tick [topic=work self.age>=35 self.job=innkeeper]
  : My first chalk mark was for a drink I've yet to see paid. I was young and soft.
  : I see that face across the square sometimes. We both look the other way.
  ask : Would you chase it, after all this time?
  b : I'd let it lie, I think. Is it much?
  : Two cups. That's why it stings. It was never the coin.

story holes_in_the_stair [topic=memories self.age>=40]
  : Our old stairwell had more air than wood in it.
  : I knew every gap by heart going up, and every one going down.
  : The morning I moved out, I didn't count. That's how I knew I was done with it.
  ask : Could you count your own steps from memory?
  b : I've never counted. Twenty, I'd guess. Do you still remember yours?
  : Thirty-one, and six of them gone. I'll remember till the ground has me.

story stone_rang [topic=weather|pastimes self.age>=25 self.likes=frosty_mornings]
  : One winter I walked the wall end to end before dawn. Frost so hard the stones rang under my paws.
  ask : Have you ever heard stone ring?
  b : Not that I know. Did it, truly?
  : Like a cup tapped on a cask. I tried at dawn again. Dead silent.

story whole_eel [topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel]
  : A carter put up a penny against me finishing a whole smoked eel at one sitting.
  : I could. I did. He paid in full, which is the part I remember best.
  ask : Would you have taken that wager, against me?
  b : Not against you. You'd only bet on a sure thing.
  : Exactly so. I don't bet on what I don't know.

story sour_sawdust [topic=work self.job=innkeeper self.age>=30]
  : The first taproom I worked had sawdust on the floor. Wet, sour sawdust, never changed.
  : I swore that if I ever had the say, it'd be straw. Fresh, every time a debt came good.
  ask : Can you smell the difference in here, now I've said it?
  b : Now you mention it. It's sweeter than most.
  : It costs. It's worth it. Every forkful.

rule @tap_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Bring your copper to the slate here. | Tabs close at the bell. No exceptions.

rule @rake_bark
when concept=bark self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Straw. Where's my rake. | That corner wants a fresh forkful.

rule @crowd_bark
when concept=bark here.day=market|festival self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Elbows in. Elbows in. | Too many bodies in here for my liking.

rule @muck_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Paws on the mat. All of you. | Half the North Road's on my boards.

rule @frost_bark
when concept=bark here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Hard frost. Good. | Cobbles white. Best morning in a month.

rule @dusk_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Lamps, then. | There goes the bell. Here we go.

dlg resident.hub : #greet#. Plain question, plain answer. | #greet#. What's wanted?
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Nothing owed. Good. | #greet#, #topic.player#. Your tab's clear, if you're asking.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late knock. Let's keep this brief. | It's after the bell. Go on.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Speak across the boards. I hear well enough. | I know your face. Say your business.
dlg resident.job [self.job=innkeeper] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I pour, I chalk, I collect. | The tap's mine. The beds upstairs aren't. I keep the cups full and the slate honest.
dlg resident.job : Work. I keep account of it. | My feet put in longer hours than my tongue.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy. Every bench taken and the slate mostly clear. | Doing well. The figures stay under my elbow.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. Drovers come, drovers go, most of them pay. | Steady. That's a figure I can live with.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : Thin. Empty benches and a slate full of names. | Poorly. No passing custom to speak of.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Off the North Road: from #world.news_from#, #world.news#. That's how it came. | A drover brought this word from #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.news [world.event_words] : The whole bar's on about #world.event_words#. | It's all #world.event_words#, cup after cup.
dlg resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : Word of robbers emptying a wagon. I'd find a bed within the walls.
dlg resident.news [world.death=recent] : A burial lately. The tap's been quieter for it.
dlg resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : A wedding this week. Good for the casks.
dlg resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : My benches have yielded precious little news. | Quiet. Ask after the evening carts.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : As I heard it: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I chalk only what I hear. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all my chalk will stretch to.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Nothing I'd repeat. | Talk's cheap. I don't deal in it.
dlg inn.greet [here.inn_helper!=yes here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. Bench, bed or a cup. Coin first. | #greet#. #inn_offer#
dlg inn.greet [topic.meeting=known here.inn_helper!=yes here.shop!=asleep] : #topic.player#. Your face I remember. Shall I fetch the slate? | Back again, #topic.player#. #inn_offer#
dlg inn.greet [here.time=night here.inn_helper!=yes here.shop!=asleep] : After dark. You'll want a bed, then. #inn_offer# | Late one. Mat first. #inn_offer#
dlg inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : #greet#. The tap's mine. #here.innkeeper# handles the beds and their keys. | I pour, nothing more. Ask #here.innkeeper# about a room.
dlg inn.rooms : Overnight I charge #here.bed_night#p. Seven nights come to #here.bed_week#p. If the upper floor's free you can take it for #here.upstairs_night#p. Paid before you climb. | Nightly rate, #here.bed_night#p. Weekly rate, #here.bed_week#p. Coin first, then the key.
dlg inn.roomed : Up the stairs. Your name's down and paid. That's a figure I can live with. | There's your bed. Paid in full. Sleep sound.
dlg inn.rest [here.lodging=yes] : Sit till you're rested. Your bed's paid for. | Take the fire. Your room's waiting when you want it.
dlg inn.rest [here.lodging!=yes] : Sit by the fire, then. A bed would do you more good. | That hearth seat costs nothing. Nobody'll move you.
dlg inn.refused : #topic.why# | Not that. #topic.why#
dlg inn.bye : #farewell#. I'll put my chalk away. | Off with you. Mind the step by the barrels.
dlg resident.bye : #farewell#. Ask for the slate if you need a reckoning. | Right. Mind the step.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=night] : Night. Keep by the gate lamps. | Night. Mind the ruts.

graft resident.hub
choice Why do you rake the straw every time? [self.job=innkeeper] -> straw
node straw
say A tab gets paid, the slate gets wiped, the floor gets fresh straw. One goes with the other. I've done it since my first cask.
mood calm
free
choice Do folk pay sooner for it? -> sooner
choice Back to it. -> hub
node sooner
say They do. Nobody likes holding up a clean sweep. Shame's a better collector than a cudgel.
choice I'll remember that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft inn.greet
choice Can I drink on credit? [self.job=innkeeper] -> credit
node credit
say Once. Your name goes on the slate, and it comes off by Restday. Miss it and you'll pay at the door from then on.
mood stern
free
choice And when I pay? -> paid
choice Back to the bar. -> greet
node paid
say Your name comes off, I rake the floor, and we're clear. A clean floor ends the account.
choice Fair enough. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
